>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Jeannel</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Stuyver</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Herv&#x000e9;</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Lunel</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1995</year><article-title>HCV infection in a rural population of the Central African Republic (CAR): evidence for three additional subtypes of genotype 4.</article-title><source>J Med Virol</source><volume>47</volume><fpage>435</fpage><lpage>437</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8636715</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000372-Jeannel1"><label>6</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jeannel</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Fretz</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Traore</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kohdjo</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Bigot</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Evidence for high genetic diversity and long-term endemicity of Hepatitis C virus genotypes 1 and 2 in West Africa.</article-title><source>J Med Virol</source><volume>55</volume><fpage>92</fpage><lpage>97</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9598927</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000372-Candotti1"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Candotti</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Temple</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Sarkodie</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Allain</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Frequent recovery and broad genotype 2 diversity characterize Hepatitis C virus infection in Ghana, West Africa.</article-title><source>J Virol</s